   "title": "Exact port of the cn class merger",
   "task": "Port the `cn` npm package (v0.2.2, ui/apps/v4/node_modules/cn, shadcn's compiled replacement for clsx+tailwind-merge that every upstream component calls) to Go as package shadcn.go/cn, byte-for-byte equivalent: same engine algorithm and the same generated tables (generate the Go tables from dist/tables.js with a script and commit the generator). Then make lib.Cn use it. Prove equivalence with a differential test: extract every class string and className combination from the upstream registry (ui/apps/v4/registry/new-york-v4 and its examples/blocks/charts) plus a randomized corpus, compute the JS results with node (commit them as testdata), and require identical Go output; add a Go fuzz test against a recorded corpus. Keep twmerge as is (it stays available). Run button's tests and the button/spinner parity references afterwards; they must still pass.",
